<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lapland War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lapland War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in northern Finland from September 1944 to April 1945. Under its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, Finland had to expel the German forces stationed in Lapland; the Germans withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, destroying Rovaniemi and much of the province's buildings, bridges and roads as they went. About a thousand Finnish soldiers were killed or went missing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lapland-war.jpg" alt="Lapland War" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sot.virk. A.Viitasalo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LapinSota.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
